\label{lem:d2gate}
At a singular place of diagram $2$ with triangle $T$ the leading solution $y_0$ has $\tau(y_0)=0$, and one of the following holds:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item $y_0$ is simple, $\theta$ is not constant, and the obstruction $\eta_2$ of the second order vanishes;
\item $y_0$ is simple, $\theta$ is constant, and the obstruction $\Omega_3$ of the third order vanishes;
\item $y_0$ is a triple point, $\theta$ and $\sigma$ are constant, and the product $b_3F_{ss}F_{TT}$ of the coefficients of the quadratic terms of its Lyapunov--Schmidt reduction vanishes;
\item $\operatorname{rank}J_0\le15$ and $y_0$ is not a triple point.
\end{enumerate}
No leading solution whose triangle is equilateral satisfies \textup{(i)}--\textup{(iv)}, at any positive masses.

We give the proof in Appendix~\ref{app:d2}. A left null vector of $J_0$ applied to the rows gives $T\tau+T^3\sigma_3$ in the local parameter $T$, whence $\tau(y_0)=0$. At a simple $y_0$ the first-order correction $y_1$ is unique. There the coefficient of $T^2$ gives $\eta_2=D\tau(y_0)\cdot y_1=0$. Here $\eta_2$ is a nonzero multiple of $(\theta_a-\theta_b)(\theta_a-\theta_c)\,w$, where $w$ is a response of the triangle block of $J_0$. It vanishes identically when $\theta$ is constant, in which case $y_1=0$ and the first coefficient that can be nonzero is $\Omega_3$, at $T^3$. At a triple point the rank is $15$ and the expansion forces $\theta$ to be constant. There the linear terms vanish after the reduction to the kernel, and the quadratic coefficients must satisfy $b_3F_{ss}F_{TT}=0$. For an equilateral triangle:
\begin{itemize}
\item at equal masses and constant $\sigma$, $|\Omega_3|\ge0.853$ for the Lagrange realization, and $b_3$, $F_{ss}$, $F_{TT}$ are nonzero for the triple realization;
\item at equal masses and nonconstant $\sigma$ the torque does not vanish;
\item at unequal masses $\theta$ is not constant and $\eta_2\ne0$ for the Lagrange realization, while the triple realization is excluded because $\theta$ would have to be constant.\qedhere
\end{itemize}

